    {"id": "V3-paper_saudi_sentiment_000", "title": "Identification of Customers Satisfaction with Popular Online Shopping Apps in Sa", "content": "Identification of Customers Satisfaction with Popular Online Shopping Apps in Saudi Arabia Using Sentiment Analysis and Topic modelling  Nada Ali Hakami, Computer Science, Jazan University, Saudi Arabia,�nmhakami@jazanu.edu.sa  DOI:�https://doi.org/10.1145/3599609.3599610  ICEEG 2023:�2023 7th International Conference on E-Commerce, E-Business and E-Government, Plymouth, United Kingdom, April 2023", "source": "saudi-sentiment-paper.docx", "dimension": "platform", "tags": []},
    {"id": "V3-paper_saudi_sentiment_001", "title": "e-commerce platforms have evolved rapidly in recent years. They allow shoppers a", "content": "e-commerce platforms have evolved rapidly in recent years. They allow shoppers around the world to buy and sell goods and services over the Internet. Understanding the factors affecting the retention of existing customers in online shopping platforms and prompting their continued engagement is crucial to the success of such platforms. In this study, factors were examined through the lens of sentiment analysis, topic modelling and user reviews from three popular online shopping apps in Saudi Arabia, namely SHEIN, Noon, and Amazon. We employed sentiment analysis by implementing and comparing the", "source": "saudi-sentiment-paper.docx", "dimension": "platform", "tags": []},
    {"id": "V3-paper_saudi_sentiment_002", "title": "CCS Concepts:�Applied computing,�Enterprise computing,�Business process manageme", "content": "CCS Concepts:�Applied computing,�Enterprise computing,�Business process management,�Business intelligence  KEYWORDS:�Online shopping,�e-commerce apps,�Customers,�User reviews,�Saudi Arabia,�Sentiment analysis,�Topic modelling,�Machine learning  ACM Reference Format:  Nada Ali Hakami. 2023. Identification of Customers Satisfaction with Popular Online Shopping Apps in Saudi Arabia Using Sentiment Analysis and Topic modelling. In�2023 7th International Conference on E-Commerce, E-Business and E-Government (ICEEG 2023), April 27-29, 2023, Plymouth, United Kingdom. ACM, New York, NY, USA, 16 Pages.", "source": "saudi-sentiment-paper.docx", "dimension": "platform", "tags": []},
    {"id": "V3-paper_saudi_sentiment_003", "title": "The proliferation of smartphones and technologies has led to a rapid growth in o", "content": "The proliferation of smartphones and technologies has led to a rapid growth in online shopping applications. According to the U.S. Census Bureau [1], retail e-commerce sales has increased from�$47.5 billion in 2011 to�$250 billion in the first quarter of 2022. Online shopping provides customers with a variety of advantages including ease and convenience, greater selection, more variations and customization, easy access to information, comprehensive product descriptions, economical prices, and price comparisons [1],[2].", "source": "saudi-sentiment-paper.docx", "dimension": "platform", "tags": []},
    {"id": "V3-paper_saudi_sentiment_004", "title": "Customer, business and market domain have benefited from the theories of Informa", "content": "Customer, business and market domain have benefited from the theories of Information Technology Acceptance, such as Information System Continuance Model (ISCM), Theory of Reasoned Action (TRA), Theory of Planned Behaviour (TPB), and Technology Acceptance Model (TAM), that identifies determinants that predict the initial acceptance (first-time use) or post acceptance (continued use) of technologies. However, one of the difficulties of using these theories is the need to collect data from large number of users such as using questionnaire. On the other hand, information and reviews posting public", "source": "saudi-sentiment-paper.docx", "dimension": "platform", "tags": []},
    {"id": "V3-paper_saudi_sentiment_005", "title": "According to [20], 93% of online shoppers rely on previous user reviews before m", "content": "According to [20], 93% of online shoppers rely on previous user reviews before making purchasing decisions. Consequently, identifying the positive and negative reviews offers important and valuable information to e-commerce market. Positive reviews highlight advantages of products that need to be maintained and improved, while negative reviews give information about problems on products that need to be tackled and resolved. The present literature shows a lack in analyzing reviews of popular online shopping apps used in Saudi Arabia. Accordingly, this study contributes to the literature by appl", "source": "saudi-sentiment-paper.docx", "dimension": "platform", "tags": []},
    {"id": "V3-paper_saudi_sentiment_006", "title": "In this paper, we evaluated the sentiment polarity of user reviews (positive or ", "content": "In this paper, we evaluated the sentiment polarity of user reviews (positive or negative) of three online shopping apps on Google Play through applying sentiment analysis (machine learning approach). For sentiment classification, we used five well-known supervised machine learning algorithms for text classification, namely Support Vector Machine (SVM), Multinomial Nai?ve Bayes (MNB), Stochastic Gradient Descent (SGD), Logistic Regression (LR), and Random Forest (RF). Afterwards, abstract topics represented in our corpus (positive reviews and negative reviews, separately) were explored using La", "source": "saudi-sentiment-paper.docx", "dimension": "platform", "tags": []},
    {"id": "V3-paper_saudi_sentiment_007", "title": "The present study is vitally important for theoretical and practical reasons. As", "content": "The present study is vitally important for theoretical and practical reasons. As far as the theoretical aspects are concerned, the present study is one of the first investigations that set out to better understand the factors that are indicative of customers\' persistence in using three common e-commerce apps in Saudi Arabia, SHEIN, noon, and Amazon. In practical terms, the results of this research help developers of e-commerce platforms to discover problems faced by their customers in order to address them and provide appropriate solutions accordingly. In addition, we offered valuable recommen", "source": "saudi-sentiment-paper.docx", "dimension": "platform", "tags": []},
    {"id": "V3-paper_saudi_sentiment_008", "title": "This section provides a review on the studies that have implemented sentiment an", "content": "This section provides a review on the studies that have implemented sentiment analysis and/or topic modelling on online shopping apps reviews (Table�1). This study set out to discover the factors which motivate/discourage shoppers to develop positive/negative intentions towards using online shopping apps exemplified by the three popular shopping apps in Saudi Arabi, namely SHEIN, Noon and Amazon. To achieve this goal, we aim to apply both sentiment analysis and topic modelling on large dataset (55,285 user reviews).  Table 1:�Summary of previous related works  Author(s)(year)/[Reference]\tResea", "source": "saudi-sentiment-paper.docx", "dimension": "platform", "tags": []},
    {"id": "V3-paper_saudi_sentiment_009", "title": "Amazon Product reviews\tApplying support vector machine (SVM), random forest and ", "content": "Amazon Product reviews\tApplying support vector machine (SVM), random forest and logistic regression (LR).\tLR and SVM were better than random forest for a binary classifier, with an F1-score of 0.84.  Haque et al. (2018) [7]\t\t\t-Applying Na�ve Bayesian, support vector machine classifier, stochastic gradient descent, linear regression, random forest and decision tree.  -Applying cross validation methods with 5 and 10 fold.\t-SVM provided the best accuracy in every dataset (cellphone & accessories data, musical instruments, and electronics) using cross validation methods with 10 fold.  -The highest", "source": "saudi-sentiment-paper.docx", "dimension": "platform", "tags": []},
    {"id": "V3-paper_saudi_sentiment_010", "title": "-SVM, Gradient Boosting, and LR models obtained accuracy of 89%, 87%, and 90%, r", "content": "-SVM, Gradient Boosting, and LR models obtained accuracy of 89%, 87%, and 90%, respectively.  Dey et al. (2020) [11]\t\t\tUsing support vector machine and naive bayes classifier.  SVM polarizes the feedback of products with a higher accuracy rate.  Rathor ET AL. (2018) [12]\t\t\tUsing support vector machine, naive bayes classifier and maximum entropy.  Singla et al. (2017)[13]\t\tMobile Phone Reviews from Amazon.\tUsing nai?ve bayes, support vector machie, and decision tree.  Patil et al. (2019) [14]\tUsing topic modelling at the first stage for calculating the accuracy of model and to identify sentimen", "source": "saudi-sentiment-paper.docx", "dimension": "platform", "tags": []},
    {"id": "V3-paper_saudi_sentiment_011", "title": "Heng et al.(2018) [15]\tUnderstand the factors that influence consumers\' online f", "content": "Heng et al.(2018) [15]\tUnderstand the factors that influence consumers\' online food purchases.\tAmazon\'s customer review data on grocery products\tTopic modeling approach,  Latent Dirichlet Allocation (LDA)\tAffording important business implications to assist potential shoppers in making better purchase decisions.  Hidayatullah et al. (2019)[16]\tDiscover topics from online shop conversation data.\tChat data from a fashion online shop, Berrybenka\t\tApplying phrase aggregation yielded better topical model results and made it easier to determine the topic label.  3�METHODOLOGY", "source": "saudi-sentiment-paper.docx", "dimension": "platform", "tags": []},
    {"id": "V3-paper_saudi_sentiment_012", "title": "The main purpose of this research is to explore the opinions of shopping apps\' c", "content": "The main purpose of this research is to explore the opinions of shopping apps\' customers and determine the positive and negative factors influencing them to use these apps. To achieve the purpose of this research, we applied the following, using Anaconda Naviagtor, Jupyter notebook (6.4.11), scikit-learn (a free software machine learning library), and the python language:  - Gathering 55,288 user reviews from three free shopping apps on Google Play Store.  - Preprocessing the data and transforming them into an efficient format though natural language processing techniques.  - Automatically ann", "source": "saudi-sentiment-paper.docx", "dimension": "platform", "tags": []},
    {"id": "V3-paper_saudi_sentiment_013", "title": "- Building and training five supervised classifiers to perform binary classifica", "content": "- Building and training five supervised classifiers to perform binary classification (positive or negative polarity) by providing them with training vectorized data.  - Evaluate the performance of the five classifiers.  - Discovering hidden topics in the underlying data set through a topic modelling approach.  3.1�Data collection", "source": "saudi-sentiment-paper.docx", "dimension": "platform", "tags": []},
    {"id": "V3-paper_saudi_sentiment_014", "title": "In October 2022, a report released by the Similarweb [4] revealed that the top t", "content": "In October 2022, a report released by the Similarweb [4] revealed that the top three free shopping apps ranking in Saudi Arabia on Google play store are the following: SHEIN, Noon, and Amazon. Reviews with scores of 1, 2 are considered negative, reviews with scores of 4 and 5 are considered positive, while reviews with a score of 3 are considered neutral. Because this study applies binary classification, we only collected reviews with scores of 1,2,4, and 5. A total of 55,288 user reviews written in English Language were collected from the three shopping apps on Google Play Store. The reviews ", "source": "saudi-sentiment-paper.docx", "dimension": "platform", "tags": []},
    {"id": "V3-paper_saudi_sentiment_015", "title": "App name\tHeadquarter\tYear founded\tTotal number of reviews  SHEIN\tSingapore\t2008\t", "content": "App name\tHeadquarter\tYear founded\tTotal number of reviews  SHEIN\tSingapore\t2008\t19,486  Noon\tUAE\t2016\t15,802  Amazon\tUSA\t1994\t20,000  3.2�Data pre-processing  Data preprocessing is considered the first step in the pipeline of a Natural Language Processing (NLP) system. It is vitally important for cleaning the noisy data and preparing it for machine learning and classification. The following are the techniques used in this paper for pre-processing the data:  . Drop Rows/Columns with Null values.  . Convert words to lowercase.  . Remove the HTML tags and URLs.  . Perform the Contractions on the ", "source": "saudi-sentiment-paper.docx", "dimension": "platform", "tags": []},
    {"id": "V3-paper_saudi_sentiment_016", "title": "After data preprocessing step, we obtained a total of 55,285 reviews for further", "content": "After data preprocessing step, we obtained a total of 55,285 reviews for further analysis.  3.3�Data annotation  To prepare the ground truth data set, we followed the approach used in [5] to automatically annotate the reviews as follows:  . Reviews with scores of 1 and 2 were converted to negative polarity.  . Reviews with scores of 4 and 5 were converted to positive polarity.  The total reviews of positive and negative sentiment polarity were 29,998 and 25,287, respectively. It was revealed that the data set was balanced with nearly half of the customers expressing positive sentiment (54.3%) ", "source": "saudi-sentiment-paper.docx", "dimension": "platform", "tags": []},
    {"id": "V3-paper_saudi_sentiment_017", "title": "TF-IDF approach is a numerical statistic used to reflect how important a word is", "content": "TF-IDF approach is a numerical statistic used to reflect how important a word is to a document in a corpus. We used the TF-IDF for extracting unigrams and vectorizing the documents (the reviews) because it gives weights to terms based on both frequency and relevance. For this purpose, the TfidfVectorizer in sklearn.feature_extraction module was used to convert a collection of raw documents to a matrix of TF-IDF features.  3.5�Sentiment classification", "source": "saudi-sentiment-paper.docx", "dimension": "platform", "tags": []},
    {"id": "V3-paper_saudi_sentiment_018", "title": "For sentiment classification, we employed five well-known supervised machine lea", "content": "For sentiment classification, we employed five well-known supervised machine learning algorithms for text classification, namely Support Vector Machine (SVM), Multinomial Nai?ve Bayes (MNB), Stochastic Gradient Descent (SGD), Logistic Regression (LR), and Random Forest (RF). With regards to training and evaluating the models, 10-fold cross validation method was applied in the present research because it provides an improvement over the holdout method.", "source": "saudi-sentiment-paper.docx", "dimension": "platform", "tags": []},
    {"id": "V3-paper_saudi_sentiment_019", "title": "Accuracy, precision, recall, and F1 score are metrics used to evaluate and compa", "content": "Accuracy, precision, recall, and F1 score are metrics used to evaluate and compare the performance of models. We employed the widely used metric, the Macro F1 score, for evaluating the performance of the models implemented in the study. The F1 score is the harmonic mean of accuracy and recall and it takes into account the false positive, false negatives, and imbalanced classes problems. Macro F1 score is the unweighted mean of the F1 scores calculated per class.  3.6�Topic modelling", "source": "saudi-sentiment-paper.docx", "dimension": "platform", "tags": []},
    {"id": "V3-paper_saudi_sentiment_020", "title": "We employed the Latent Dirichlet Allocation (LDA), a popular topic modeling meth", "content": "We employed the Latent Dirichlet Allocation (LDA), a popular topic modeling method used to extract topics from a given corpus. To perform LDA, we tokenized the reviews, converted the tokenized text into corpus and dictionary, built LDA model, visualized topics for interpretability, and computed coherence score. The topic modelling technique was applied on the positive and negative reviews, separately. After experiments, we determined 7 and 6 as the satisfactory number of topics in the underlying positive and negative user reviews, respectively. The coherence score using \"u mass\" was -3.245 and", "source": "saudi-sentiment-paper.docx", "dimension": "platform", "tags": []},
    {"id": "V3-paper_saudi_sentiment_021", "title": "After training and testing the five models, we compared their performance to fin", "content": "After training and testing the five models, we compared their performance to find out the best classifier for classifying the reviews. It can be seen in Table�3�that all the five classifiers outperformed the random baseline of 50%. The best Macro F1 score was obtained from the SGD classifier with 91.88% followed by LR, SVM, RF and MNB with 91.18%, 90.82%, 90.74%, and 85.04%, respectively. Additionally, SGD provided the highest predictive accuracy among the other classifiers with 92.71%.  Table 3:�Cross validation results  Classifier\tMean-Accuracy(?)\tMean-F1 Macro(?)  SVM\t91.8048 (�0.0497)\t90.8", "source": "saudi-sentiment-paper.docx", "dimension": "platform", "tags": []},
    {"id": "V3-paper_saudi_sentiment_022", "title": "The cloud visualization of positive and negative reviews are exemplified in Figu", "content": "The cloud visualization of positive and negative reviews are exemplified in Figure�1. Some of the most frequent words shown in the cloud visualization of the positive reviews were: great app, good quality, good service, easy to use, fast delivery, price, time. On the other hand, the cloud visualization of the negative reviews displays words on refund, return, shipping, price, customer service, bad, slow, frustrating, cancel, change, expensive, update.  Figure 1:�Cloud visualization of positive reviews (left) and negative reviews (right)  4.2�Topic modelling", "source": "saudi-sentiment-paper.docx", "dimension": "platform", "tags": []},
    {"id": "V3-paper_saudi_sentiment_023", "title": "The results of applying LDA on the positive and negative reviews revealed variou", "content": "The results of applying LDA on the positive and negative reviews revealed various topics discussed by the apps\' customers in relation to their experiences in online shopping. Table�4and 5 demonstrate the top keywords appearing in the underlying corpus and their weights. Topics are words with highest probability of relevance to a topic, and the numbers are the probabilities of words belonging to topic distribution. Topics extracted from the positive and negative reviews by means of the LDA method along with their sub-topics are shown in Table�6�and 7, respectively.  Table 4:�LDA results on the ", "source": "saudi-sentiment-paper.docx", "dimension": "platform", "tags": []},
    {"id": "V3-paper_saudi_sentiment_024", "title": "1\tGreat(0.114),�nan(0.068),�app(0.024),�easy(0.019),�shopping(0.013),�experience", "content": "1\tGreat(0.114),�nan(0.068),�app(0.024),�easy(0.019),�shopping(0.013),�experience(0.013),�price(0.013),�always(0.011),�get(0.011),�good(0.010)  2\tGood(0.051),�app(0.032),�best(0.022),�order(0.020),�quality(0.019),�shopping(0.018),�fast(0.015),�easy(0.013),�item(0.013),�online(0.010)  3\tGood(0.105),�love(0.048),�app(0.043),�clothes(0.021),�great(0.018),�price(0.017),�quality(0.016),�easy(0.015),�product(0.015),�itis(0.014)  4\tLove(0.045),�good(0.031),�service(0.024),�amazon(0.021),�experience(0.019),�like(0.016),�it is(0.012),�shopping(0.012),�need(0.011),�shop(0.011)  5\tNice(0.080),�excellent(0", "source": "saudi-sentiment-paper.docx", "dimension": "platform", "tags": []},
    {"id": "V3-paper_saudi_sentiment_025", "title": "Topic Distribution No.\tWords with probabilities of their belonging to the topic ", "content": "Topic Distribution No.\tWords with probabilities of their belonging to the topic distribution  0\tNan(0.041),�app(0.028),�bad(0.023),�service(0.017),�delivery(0.016),�order(0.013),�shipping(0.012),�day(0.011),�get(0.010),�time(0.009)  1\tOrder(0.019),�app(0.019),�money(0.012),�delivery(0.011),�get(0.010),�item(0.010),�service(0.009),�customer(0.009),�day(0.009),�clothes(0.008)  2\tApp(0.028),�item(0.017),�good(0.017),�time(0.012),�amazon(0.012),�customer(0.011),�return(0.011),�order(0.010),�service(0.010),�donot(0.010)  3\tApp(0.018),�size(0.016),�order(0.015),�product(0.013),�good(0.013),�clothes(", "source": "saudi-sentiment-paper.docx", "dimension": "platform", "tags": []},
    {"id": "V3-paper_saudi_sentiment_026", "title": "5\tApp(0.018),�delivery(0.015),�nan(0.013),�donot(0.010),�customer(0.009),�amazon", "content": "5\tApp(0.018),�delivery(0.015),�nan(0.013),�donot(0.010),�customer(0.009),�amazon(0.009),�service(0.008),�time(0.008),�like(0.008),�card(0.008)  Table 6:�Topics/sub-topics extracted from the positive user reviews  Topic\tTopic description\tSub-Topics  (0, 5)- Fast and reliable delivery\tDelivering items to customers in a quick time, at the right time and at the right place(reliable delivery).  .\tFast delivery, accurate estimate of the delivery, package safety and return easiness  1- Easy shopping\tEasy and convenient online shopping experience.\tConvenient shopping, ease of use of apps, saving time,", "source": "saudi-sentiment-paper.docx", "dimension": "platform", "tags": []},
    {"id": "V3-paper_saudi_sentiment_027", "title": "3- Item price\tFinding products in reasonable and affordable prices.\tAffordable p", "content": "3- Item price\tFinding products in reasonable and affordable prices.\tAffordable prices  4- Good services\tGood and helpful services provided such as customer services, shipping services, delivery services, follow-up services.\tResponsiveness, reliability, follow-up service, tracking service. system quality, information quality  6- Item size\tObtaining an appropriate size of item.\tAccurate size, offering plus size, providing size charts & measurements  5�DISCUSSION", "source": "saudi-sentiment-paper.docx", "dimension": "platform", "tags": []},
    {"id": "V3-paper_saudi_sentiment_028", "title": "This research was conducted with the purpose of examining the effectiveness of c", "content": "This research was conducted with the purpose of examining the effectiveness of common three online shopping apps in Saudi Arabia based on user reviews. Our results showed that SGD classifier yielded the highest Macro F1 and accuracy with 91.88% and 92.71%, respectively. This finding concurs with a result published by [5] who had shown that SGD achieved the best F1 score (89.42%) for predicting the polarity of mental health apps reviews.", "source": "saudi-sentiment-paper.docx", "dimension": "platform", "tags": []},
    {"id": "V3-paper_saudi_sentiment_029", "title": "Topics discussed by customers in the underlying reviews were extracted with the ", "content": "Topics discussed by customers in the underlying reviews were extracted with the help of LDA method. Applying the LDA on the positive reviews produced the themes: fast and reliable delivery, easy shopping, quality of product/order/shopping item price, good services, and item size (Table�6). The results obtained from applying LDA on the negative reviews showed the topics: poor services, refund/money issues, return products, size of products, Apps updates, and late delivery(Table�7). The following sections present sample comments on topics extracted from the positive and negative reviews.  Table ", "source": "saudi-sentiment-paper.docx", "dimension": "platform", "tags": []},
    {"id": "V3-paper_saudi_sentiment_030", "title": "1- Refund/Money issues\tProblems related to receiving refunds for returned/cancel", "content": "1- Refund/Money issues\tProblems related to receiving refunds for returned/cancelled orders.\tDelayed refund, no refund allowed, refunding through wallet only, enforce refund through the app  2- Return products\tProblems related to returning unfitted items such as poor return policies, slow return processes.\tDelayed return, lack of clarity in the return policy, Lack of clarity in the type of sellers, lack of clarity in the return option in the application, charging fees for returning items  3- Product size\tObtaining inappropriately sized products.\tInaccurate size, not providing size charts & meas", "source": "saudi-sentiment-paper.docx", "dimension": "platform", "tags": []},
    {"id": "V3-paper_saudi_sentiment_031", "title": "5.1.1�Fast and Reliable Delivery.�According to customers, fast and reliable deli", "content": "5.1.1�Fast and Reliable Delivery.�According to customers, fast and reliable delivery and shipping is an influential and motivational factor that might affect buyers\' decision in their shopping experience. Some customers expressed their willingness to obtain an accurate estimate of the delivery period (R1, R2):  \"Very helpful accurate delivery date\"�[R1]  \"Relatively good quality for the price. Reliable shipments. Responsive customer service. Men\'s shoes had trouble fitting on many occasions. Jewelry offers are nice.\"�[R2]  Below are sample comments from users reviews regarding the fast deliver", "source": "saudi-sentiment-paper.docx", "dimension": "platform", "tags": []},
    {"id": "V3-paper_saudi_sentiment_032", "title": "\"Pros- 1) Quick delivery, 2) Most of our search things are available on sale lis", "content": "\"Pros- 1) Quick delivery, 2) Most of our search things are available on sale list, 3)Customer care response is good, 4)Tracking option available on our order, 5)Packing is in proper condition, 6)Affordable price.\"[R5]  \"Clothing either comes on time or before date given, clothes have been of good quality and fit. Returns are quick and simple if you chose the easiest form of courier.\"�[R6]  Although customers look for fast delivery, especially for high-value goods, late delivery does not affect their behavioral intention to use online shopping[18]. On the other hand, receiving goods at the righ", "source": "saudi-sentiment-paper.docx", "dimension": "platform", "tags": []},
    {"id": "V3-paper_saudi_sentiment_033", "title": "Also, the ease of use of apps is an important aspect in online shopping (R8):  \"", "content": "Also, the ease of use of apps is an important aspect in online shopping (R8):  \"I\'ve ordered a few times now and I have to say that the app is quite easy to use . Items have been terrific and orders have come quickly. I have had no issues at all and will continue to use it for my shopping . Christmas shopping ...is done ! Thank you SHEIN\"�[R8]  Some customers held the opinion that shopping online is easy for several reasons, such as saving time, shopping at any time, saving transportation expenses (R9), avoiding crowds (R10):  \"Second time using but A very convenient service especially for the", "source": "saudi-sentiment-paper.docx", "dimension": "platform", "tags": []},
    {"id": "V3-paper_saudi_sentiment_034", "title": "Opinions regarding the ease of use were expected as it has been shown that the p", "content": "Opinions regarding the ease of use were expected as it has been shown that the perceived ease of use of technological interfaces in online shopping sites is a strong predictor of the shopper\'s attitude towards online shopping [17].  5.1.3�Quality of Product/Order/Shopping.�Many customers believed that the quality of products and orders is an important factor affecting their attitudes towards online shopping. Quality in this respect means the company deals products with high quality, provides various products, and supports high product availability [19], (R11,R12,R13):  \"This is one of the best", "source": "saudi-sentiment-paper.docx", "dimension": "platform", "tags": []},
    {"id": "V3-paper_saudi_sentiment_035", "title": "\"The application is easy to use and many products range are available.\"�[R13]  5", "content": "\"The application is easy to use and many products range are available.\"�[R13]  5.1.4�Item Price.�Many consumers were eager to buy goods at a lower prices, as reflected in the user reviews:  \"Lot of styles to choose from and affordable prices.\"�[R14]  \"I haven\'t ordered yet but the prices are amazing and my daughter buys clothes from here and she loves them\"�[R15]  5.1.5�Good Services.�According to [19], \"Service quality in the traditional IS environment is based on the perspective that the organization is composed of multiple processes with the goal of providing the customer with high-quality ", "source": "saudi-sentiment-paper.docx", "dimension": "platform", "tags": []},
    {"id": "V3-paper_saudi_sentiment_036", "title": "Responsiveness\t\"New to Shein and received my order which was of a high quality a", "content": "Responsiveness\t\"New to Shein and received my order which was of a high quality and excellent value. Customer services answered quickly on the online app.\" [R16]  Reliability\t\"Relatively good quality for the price. Reliable shipments. Responsive customer service.�Men\'s shoes had trouble fitting on many occasions. Jewelry offers are nice.\"�[R17]  Follow-up services\t\"First of all, thank you very much for the quick response, verification and follow-up Second .. This is the first experience of buying from Noon site .. And I\'m satisfied with my experience with it , God willing, the site of Noon will", "source": "saudi-sentiment-paper.docx", "dimension": "platform", "tags": []},
    {"id": "V3-paper_saudi_sentiment_037", "title": "System and information quality can be considered in this respect. System quality", "content": "System and information quality can be considered in this respect. System quality and information quality have been described by [19] as follows:  \"System quality describes the measures of Web sites as information processing system and taps the engineering-oriented performance characteristics such as operational efficiency and appearance\".  \"The most commonly used items for information quality are accuracy, currency, complete- ness, timeliness, and understandability\".", "source": "saudi-sentiment-paper.docx", "dimension": "platform", "tags": []},
    {"id": "V3-paper_saudi_sentiment_038", "title": "System quality can be measured with metrics such as design, navigation, response", "content": "System quality can be measured with metrics such as design, navigation, response time, system security, system availability, functionality, error free transaction, and multimedia [19]. On the other hand, metrics such as contents variety, complete information, detail information, accurate information, timely information, reliable information, and appropriate format are used for assessing the quality of information [19]. Table�9�shows sample comments from the user reviews on some aspects of system and information quality.  Table 9:�Sample comments related to system and information quality metric", "source": "saudi-sentiment-paper.docx", "dimension": "platform", "tags": []},
    {"id": "V3-paper_saudi_sentiment_039", "title": "System quality/Navigation\t\"Regarding App only... a good and consistent navigatio", "content": "System quality/Navigation\t\"Regarding App only... a good and consistent navigation experience. Detailed product and field information. Thank you\"�[R24]  \"App is comprehensive, easy to navigate & Reliable.\"�[R25]  System quality/multimedia\t\"It\'s a very good app. Things shown in the picture almost resemble the actual ones. Deliveries are on time. I have had a good experience shopping with noon so far.\"�[R26]  System quality/ functionality\t\"Functional and elegant company and very attractive and well-designed app. The only con is the higher prices of its products compared to other companies.\"�[R27]", "source": "saudi-sentiment-paper.docx", "dimension": "platform", "tags": []},
    {"id": "V3-paper_saudi_sentiment_040", "title": "Information quality/accurate information\t\"Easy to use, accurate search and fast ", "content": "Information quality/accurate information\t\"Easy to use, accurate search and fast delivery.\"�[R30]  \"The app is super smooth and organized. Just needs more accurate filtering options and sorting choices.\" [R31]  \"Wonderful application, easy to use, support many payment options and fast, accurate information and delivery\"[R32]  5.1.6�Item Size.�As shown by many user reviews, consumer satisfaction with online shopping increases when receiving items/products of accurate and correct size:", "source": "saudi-sentiment-paper.docx", "dimension": "platform", "tags": []},
    {"id": "V3-paper_saudi_sentiment_041", "title": "\"Shien is a really good place to shop at, because they\'re clothes come in very g", "content": "\"Shien is a really good place to shop at, because they\'re clothes come in very good material. They also come as the right size, the clothes are the exact same as they look on the website. I also like how shien orders come early sometimes, or it wouldn\'t take too long. I really recommend shien to order clothes from, I haven\'t ordered anything else but I know clothes can be really good to order off of shien.�(:\"�[R21]  One customer expressed the benefit of offering items of plus size:  \"I love this app it has a lot of variety things for plus size girls\"�[R22]  Providing size charts and measureme", "source": "saudi-sentiment-paper.docx", "dimension": "platform", "tags": []},
    {"id": "V3-paper_saudi_sentiment_042", "title": "5.2.1�Poor Services.�A customer complained about the quality of goods received a", "content": "5.2.1�Poor Services.�A customer complained about the quality of goods received as well as items not delivered:  \"Bad service....one of the worst online services. Delivery items not good....all are cheating. I ordered some items. It\'s not delivered. Seller cheats me. My money is gone. Don\'t order next time...in Amazon Any items. Worst service.\"�[R34]  Another customer expressed his dissatisfaction with reliability of delivery and following the instructions for delivering the products:  \"Unreliable deliveries. If I order something to come on a Friday, don\'t deliver it Thursday. And don\'t just le", "source": "saudi-sentiment-paper.docx", "dimension": "platform", "tags": []},
    {"id": "V3-paper_saudi_sentiment_043", "title": "\"The package was marked as delivered in the app, but nobody showed up or called.", "content": "\"The package was marked as delivered in the app, but nobody showed up or called. The only option I am given is a refund, but since it was a product with a discount I have to pay more than initially if I were to order again. Looks like Amazon is just baiting me into buying a product at a higher price than initially offered.\" [R36]  Door delivery is the most important factor affecting buyers\' intentions to continue using online shopping [22]. However, according to (R37), one delivery representative refused to deliver orders to a customer\'s home:  \"Worst delivery service of amazon. Delivery guy r", "source": "saudi-sentiment-paper.docx", "dimension": "platform", "tags": []},
    {"id": "V3-paper_saudi_sentiment_044", "title": "\"Very bad experience, They don\'t have real time tracking or tracking details of ", "content": "\"Very bad experience, They don\'t have real time tracking or tracking details of delivery persons once the shipment is out for delivery. I called them 3-4times to get driver contact as I have flight to catch\"�[R38]  One shopper held the opinion that a customer service representative was unable to react and respond to his enquires:  \"Their customer service is very rude, From the UK right? They really love to hang up on you while you are telling them the problem that\'s happening from the app and website. Very very rude! If you can\'t solve them, transfer me to the correct department, what is your ", "source": "saudi-sentiment-paper.docx", "dimension": "platform", "tags": []},
    {"id": "V3-paper_saudi_sentiment_045", "title": "\"Search and navigation is PAINFULLY worthless. Search results in nothing but unr", "content": "\"Search and navigation is PAINFULLY worthless. Search results in nothing but unrelated items. Prices are hidden and false scarcity tactics abound\"�[R40]  5.2.2�Refund/Money Issues.�A few customers highlighted the issue with the delay in refunds, for example:  \"They gave me 1 business day to return a package and it\'s been a month since I sent it and still no refund or anything. I do not recommend this app for anything\"�[R41]  Many customers did not like refunding money through the wallet, for example:  \"did not like that refund could only be issued via internal wallet with Shien and it was not ", "source": "saudi-sentiment-paper.docx", "dimension": "platform", "tags": []},
    {"id": "V3-paper_saudi_sentiment_046", "title": "\"Twice they delivered to the wrong address. They won\'t refund the 60 dollars. So", "content": "\"Twice they delivered to the wrong address. They won\'t refund the 60 dollars. So I lose 60 dollars because their drivers can\'t follow instruction or maps.\"�[R43]  A customer complained that he was forced to download the application to get a refund:  \"Had to install this to request refund from Amazon. Unethical manipulation to get users to install an unwanted app.\"�[R44]  5.2.3�Return Products.�For any e-commerce company, return and refund policy must be presented in a clear, concise manner to avoid misunderstandings. One of the customers criticized the lack of clarity in the return policy:  \"T", "source": "saudi-sentiment-paper.docx", "dimension": "platform", "tags": []},
    {"id": "V3-paper_saudi_sentiment_047", "title": "\"Amazon has the worst return policy ever and I don\'t recommend anyone to buy any", "content": "\"Amazon has the worst return policy ever and I don\'t recommend anyone to buy any car parts from them and I will not purchase anything else from them\"�[R46]  Retailers charge their customers to return items bought online, as stated by one customer:  \"They charge for returning the product also they refund the remaining amount after so long that too into Shein wallet\"�[R47]  In this regard, one of the customers expressed his inability to distinguish between the third-party sellers of Amazon products from the inventory of other sellers on Amazon, which in turns affected his ability to return the i", "source": "saudi-sentiment-paper.docx", "dimension": "platform", "tags": []},
    {"id": "V3-paper_saudi_sentiment_048", "title": "\"I bought a television. An Amazon fire TV. Amazon doesn\'t do returns for 3rd par", "content": "\"I bought a television. An Amazon fire TV. Amazon doesn\'t do returns for 3rd party sellers. It came from Best Buy. They won\'t do exchanges or returns so I\'m out of almost 300$. Since they don\'t show which items are 3rd party sellers, I quit Amazon prime ... again. Both times are because of the customer support. The first time they tried to get money for re-stocking fees for something that came directly from the seller and refused to allow me and seller to communicate.\"�[R48]  A few customers mentioned that return option was not clear in the design of the app:  \"Useless app. Order is taking age", "source": "saudi-sentiment-paper.docx", "dimension": "platform", "tags": []},
    {"id": "V3-paper_saudi_sentiment_049", "title": "\"I spent more time having to return broken stuff from them that would be quicker", "content": "\"I spent more time having to return broken stuff from them that would be quicker to shop in store, definitely need to work on their quality control\" [R50]  5.2.4�Product Size.�Many shoppers have identified the problem of receiving wrong/inaccurate sized products. This finding is consistent with a study by Narvar [21] that reported that sizing and fit were the most common reason for returning online orders. Below is a sample comment from a user review regarding sizing issue in online orders:  \"Affordable quality fashion e-commerce. Exceptional cool designs where you can\'t find elsewhere. The on", "source": "saudi-sentiment-paper.docx", "dimension": "platform", "tags": []},
    {"id": "V3-paper_saudi_sentiment_050", "title": "Some customers stated the problem of not providing size measurements, for exampl", "content": "Some customers stated the problem of not providing size measurements, for example:  \"The app shows cute clothes but has inconsistent sizing & offers, no way to search for measurements to mitigate their inconsistency.\"�[R52]  5.2.5�App updates.�Some customers have had issues using the app after the update as shown in Table�10.  Table 10:�Sample comments related to app updates issues  Issue\tSample comments  Slow app\t\"New update is so slow it\'s unusable. Every scroll or swipe takes 10 seconds to catch up. None of my other apps are doing this. It\'s been a week now and nothing has changed. Guess I ", "source": "saudi-sentiment-paper.docx", "dimension": "platform", "tags": []},
    {"id": "V3-paper_saudi_sentiment_051", "title": "Incompatibility\t\"Was working fine, till an auto-update a month or two ago. Now i", "content": "Incompatibility\t\"Was working fine, till an auto-update a month or two ago. Now it only says it\'s incompatible with my device!? I have not changed anything, the app auto-updated! PLEASE get this working again, I tried clearing/reinstalling, check OS for any updates but all is updated, but still says same thing. I use this app a lot and would like to get it back!\"�[R54]  Removing App data\t\"App update destroyed everything. Doesn\'t show recent orders. Filters is a mess\"�[R55]  \"With the new update its deleted all my wish list I wanted to get and now can\'t remember any of it\"�[R56]", "source": "saudi-sentiment-paper.docx", "dimension": "platform", "tags": []},
    {"id": "V3-paper_saudi_sentiment_052", "title": "Difficulty in searching items\t\"The latest update made searching for specific ite", "content": "Difficulty in searching items\t\"The latest update made searching for specific items difficult! I tried to give it a few weeks and see if I just needed time to get used to it, but no! Search results are broad and fairly unrelated to what I\'m actually searching for. Trying the filter isn\'t much help either. Trying to filter by brand still shows cheap look-alikes. Trying to filter by price range shows expensive look-alikes, like you\'re trying to HIDE the items I actually want to buy!\"�[R57]  App crash\t\"App constantly crashes/locks up after current update. This has been going on for 2 weeks. You wo", "source": "saudi-sentiment-paper.docx", "dimension": "platform", "tags": []},
    {"id": "V3-paper_saudi_sentiment_053", "title": "5.2.6�Late Delivery.�It was reported that \"69% of consumers are much less or les", "content": "5.2.6�Late Delivery.�It was reported that \"69% of consumers are much less or less likely to shop with a retailer in the future if an item they purchased is not delivered within two days of the date promised\" [23]. The user reviews showed that many buyers were affected by late deliveries:  \"Product are all good legit. The problem is the delivery time. So delayed, always waste my time waiting. Iam also working and need rest. Iam not always available at any time, that is why there is schedule in this apps. So I hope you respect also our time. I hope this will be fixed..\"�[R59]  \"Delivery times ar", "source": "saudi-sentiment-paper.docx", "dimension": "platform", "tags": []},
    {"id": "V3-paper_saudi_sentiment_054", "title": "\"Don\'t waste your money on prime the deliveries never come on time. Again Amazon", "content": "\"Don\'t waste your money on prime the deliveries never come on time. Again Amazon gives me a delivery date and it fails to get here on the date promised. Save your money you will get your order the same time you would with regular shipping. If this was a time thing I could understand but it\'s a continuous trend.\"�[R61]  In light of the findings of this study, some recommendations were put forward to e-commerce providers and apps developers to adopt strategies which could increase shopper loyalty for online shopping use (Table�11).  Table 11:�Some recommendation for e-commerce providers  Factor\t", "source": "saudi-sentiment-paper.docx", "dimension": "platform", "tags": []},
    {"id": "V3-paper_saudi_sentiment_055", "title": "- Follow up after the problem has been solved.  - Train delivery drivers on:  - ", "content": "- Follow up after the problem has been solved.  - Train delivery drivers on:  - Customer service  - Using your delivery software  - Process and professionalism  - Health and safety training  - Give customers the opportunity to rate delivery drivers and vice versa.  System/Information quality\t    - Enrich product content and description.  - Invest heavily in high-quality site search functionality.  - Let consumers try on products virtually.  - Help customers by providing comparisons of specific features of different similar products.  - Use charts and tables for effective products comparison.  ", "source": "saudi-sentiment-paper.docx", "dimension": "platform", "tags": []},
    {"id": "V3-paper_saudi_sentiment_056", "title": "Refund/return issues\t    - Make sure your return policy is very clear.  - Keep t", "content": "Refund/return issues\t    - Make sure your return policy is very clear.  - Keep the return and refund policy terms simple and clear.  - Realize the need for free return shipping.  - Stipulate a realistic return deadline.  - Make the refund swift.  - Give customers the flexibility to select between different refunding methods: bank, wallet, etc.  Size issues\t    - Check out why do customers have trouble finding the right size online?  - Give measurable sizes in numbers, and remember that Small, Medium, Large, etc. are different from a brand to brand.  - Build a size guide using a variety of imag", "source": "saudi-sentiment-paper.docx", "dimension": "platform", "tags": []},
    {"id": "V3-paper_saudi_sentiment_057", "title": "App updates issues\t    - Check out problems faced by your customers after updati", "content": "App updates issues\t    - Check out problems faced by your customers after updating apps.  - Accordingly, give customers a user guide on how to fix the problems they are facing.  Customer engagement\tIntroduce gamification techniques such as:  - Allow customers earn points for certain actions, such as placing an order, leaving a review, etc.  - Use leaderboards to motivate shoppers to purchase products or leave helpful product reviews [24].  - Support enjoyable product recommendations through providing fun quizzes to direct your customers to the right product for them.  - Offer only one initial ", "source": "saudi-sentiment-paper.docx", "dimension": "platform", "tags": []},
    {"id": "V3-paper_saudi_sentiment_058", "title": "In this study, we applied sentiment analysis and topic modelling approaches with", "content": "In this study, we applied sentiment analysis and topic modelling approaches with the aim to explore customers\' opinion regarding three popular online shopping apps in Saudi Arabia. In sentiment analysis, we implemented and compared the performance of five machine learning classifiers and found out that SGD was the best performing classifier in terms of Macro F1 and accuracy at 91.88% and 92.71%, respectively. After conducting the sentiment analysis, the topic modelling approach was adopted on the positive and negative user reviews, by means of LDA method. Results from topic modeling showed the", "source": "saudi-sentiment-paper.docx", "dimension": "platform", "tags": []},
    {"id": "V3-paper_saudi_sentiment_059", "title": "This research is beneficial for future studies on e-commerce, particularly for u", "content": "This research is beneficial for future studies on e-commerce, particularly for understanding customer attitudes towards online shopping and the factors that influence their perspective. Furthermore, our findings can serve as a useful reference for e-commerce business to improve customers satisfaction, service quality and increase the sales. Drawing upon the obtained results, recommendations were provided for e-commerce providers. In future work, we plan to implement aspect-based sentiment analysis techniques which is a fine-grained sentiment analysis task, that detects the sentiment polarity t", "source": "saudi-sentiment-paper.docx", "dimension": "platform", "tags": []},
