    {"id": "PLATFORM-6644d4fa2151b_453453-002", "title": "Source: Euromonitor International", "content": "Source: Euromonitor International\nNote:*MENA includes Algeria, Egypt, Iran, Israel, Jordan, Kuwait, Lebanon, Morocco, Oman, Qatar, the KSA, Tunisia, and the UAEIntroduction- Executive Summary \nE-commerce Snapshot in MENA* region\nGrowing investments in digital infrastructure, stronger regulations and rising consumer confidence \nin digital payments is likely to drive an over-5x growth in e-commerce over the decade, 2018-282018\n2028Total E-commerce \nMarket Value \nE-commerce Penetration E-commerce Penetration E-commerce PenetrationTotal E-commerce \nMarket Value 2018-23\nCAGR %2023-28\nCAGR %9.5\n1.4%", "source": "platform/6644d4fa2151b_453453458374592745.pdf", "dimension": "platform", "tags": []},
    {"id": "PLATFORM-6644d4fa2151b_453453-003", "title": "Source: Euromonitor International", "content": "Source: Euromonitor International\nNote: *MENA for category performance analysis includes only the UAE, KSA, Egypt, and Morocco\nHistoric data: current prices, y-o-y exchange rateExecutive Summary – E-commerce in MENA Region\nMost product categories see strong growth, driven by wide product offering, extensive promotions \nand rising consumer confidence in online purchases post COVID-19\nTotal E -commerce Market Size by Industry across key markets in MENA * \nUSD billion (2018/2023/2028) and CAGR % (2018-2023/2023-2028)\n30%37%48%\n28%\n24%35%\n27%37%38%\n1%11% 11%16%\n10%\n7%14%\n8%10%13% 13%\n0%20%40%60%\n ", "source": "platform/6644d4fa2151b_453453458374592745.pdf", "dimension": "platform", "tags": []},
    {"id": "PLATFORM-6644d4fa2151b_453453-004", "title": "Top five trends shaping the MENA e-commerce market prioritizing customer conveni", "content": "Top five trends shaping the MENA e-commerce market prioritizing customer convenience and seamless shopping experiencesExecutive Summary – Industry Trends –  MENA Region\n•  The omnichannel \napproach is gaining \ntraction as consumers \nseek seamless \nshopping experiences.  \n•  This trend, fueled by \nthe use of promo \ncodes, discounts, \nand loyalty points,  is \nexpected to grow with \nthe rising demand for \nfast delivery.•  The MENA region is \nexperiencing a surge \nin digital payments,  \nsuch as E-wallets, P2P \npayments, and BNPL \nservices, driven by \ngrowing trust in their \nsecurity. \n•  BNPL serv", "source": "platform/6644d4fa2151b_453453458374592745.pdf", "dimension": "platform", "tags": []},
