    {"id": "PLATFORM-商业生态系统视角下出口型跨境电商企业的海-053", "title": "The two of them analysed the performance of enterprise development based on ente", "content": "The two of them analysed the performance of enterprise development based on enterprise ecological niche theory by applying enterprise ecological niche theory and enterprise  growth theory,  and gave solutions [3] . Yan An and Da Qingli (2005), by analysing   and   comparing   the    differences   and   similarities   between   enterprise ecological niche and biological ecological niche, combined with the characteristics of the  enterprise,  and  summarized  how  to   use  enterprise  ecological  niche   [4] .  Li Dongliang (2008), based on the ecological niche theory, viewed the enterprise as ", "source": "platform/商业生态系统视角下出口型跨境电商企业的海外战略分析_孙智佳.docx", "dimension": "platform", "tags": []},
    {"id": "PLATFORM-商业生态系统视角下出口型跨境电商企业的海-054", "title": "The  research  results  of  domestic   scholars  on  the   application  of  busi", "content": "The  research  results  of  domestic   scholars  on  the   application  of  business ecosystem in the field of cross-border e-commerce in recent years are as follows: Guo Hailing, Ma Hongyu, and Zhu Jiaqi (2021) constructed a cross-border e-commerce", "source": "platform/商业生态系统视角下出口型跨境电商企业的海外战略分析_孙智佳.docx", "dimension": "platform", "tags": []},
    {"id": "PLATFORM-商业生态系统视角下出口型跨境电商企业的海-055", "title": "information service ecosystem conceptual model on the basis ofan in-depth analys", "content": "information service ecosystem conceptual model on the basis ofan in-depth analysis of cross-border  e-commerce  information  service ecosystem constituents as  well as interactions between the constituent elements, which can provide theoretical basis for further   improving  the  quality  of  cross-border  e-commerce   information  service organisations   in  terms   of  information   service   quality  and  efficiency  provides theoretical basis [6] . Tongyan Fu and Huiying Du (2023) proposed the development trend of cross-border e-commerce ecosystem at home and abroad from the research of cr", "source": "platform/商业生态系统视角下出口型跨境电商企业的海外战略分析_孙智佳.docx", "dimension": "platform", "tags": []},
    {"id": "PLATFORM-商业生态系统视角下出口型跨境电商企业的海-056", "title": "In summary, it can be seen from the above analysis, our scholars in cross-border", "content": "In summary, it can be seen from the above analysis, our scholars in cross-border e-commerce business ecosystem research results, although more abundant, especially in recent years, the field of research continues to expand, the object of research to academic theory to explore the main, for the cross-border e-commerce platform from the perspective of the business ecosystem of the business case study of enterprises has not yet a relatively systematic and adequate discussion of the research. Based on this text,  we  will  take  Temu  and  SHEIN  platforms  as  cases,  and  from  the  Business Eco", "source": "platform/商业生态系统视角下出口型跨境电商企业的海外战略分析_孙智佳.docx", "dimension": "platform", "tags": []},
    {"id": "PLATFORM-商业生态系统视角下出口型跨境电商企业的海-057", "title": "their strategies according to the ecological environment and their own changes, ", "content": "their strategies according to the ecological environment and their own changes, so as to make them maintain a high degree of resilience and a high degree of adaptive and evolutionary  capacity.", "source": "platform/商业生态系统视角下出口型跨境电商企业的海外战略分析_孙智佳.docx", "dimension": "platform", "tags": []},
    {"id": "PLATFORM-商业生态系统视角下出口型跨境电商企业的海-058", "title": "Business Ecosystem Theory posits that organizations,  like species in a biologic", "content": "Business Ecosystem Theory posits that organizations,  like species in a biological ecosystem, occupy specific ecological niches within markets. A niche represents a distinct segment or position within a  market where an organization can thrive and fulfill unique customer needs. Organizations seek to identify and exploit niches that offer them  a  competitive  advantage  and  protect  them  from  direct  competition.  A business   ecosystem   is   a   community   of  interest   based   on   inter-organisational interactions  formed  by  many  sub-companies   to  adapt  to  a  competitive   mark", "source": "platform/商业生态系统视角下出口型跨境电商企业的海外战略分析_孙智佳.docx", "dimension": "platform", "tags": []},
    {"id": "PLATFORM-商业生态系统视角下出口型跨境电商企业的海-059", "title": "The business ecosystem model is a way to build a business ecosystem to obtain th", "content": "The business ecosystem model is a way to build a business ecosystem to obtain the benefits of   investment or cooperation, and to combine the business model, profit\n\n3   1996 James F. Moore, The Demise of Competition - Leadership  and Strategy in the Age of Business Ecosystems", "source": "platform/商业生态系统视角下出口型跨境电商企业的海外战略分析_孙智佳.docx", "dimension": "platform", "tags": []},
    {"id": "PLATFORM-商业生态系统视角下出口型跨境电商企业的海-060", "title": "model and operation model with actual operation. At present, scholars at home an", "content": "model and operation model with actual operation. At present, scholars at home and abroad  do  not  have  a  clear  conclusion  on  the  business   ecosystem  model,   but companies such as Intel, Qualcomm, Apple, Google and Disney, as well as thousands of participants in their respective business ecosystems, are collectively demonstrating the structure of the business ecosystem model - a distributed and enhanced structure, a system  architecture  with  both  absolute  and  relative  comparative  advantages   -  to enterprises.   The   Business   Ecosystem   Model   is   a   distributed   and  ", "source": "platform/商业生态系统视角下出口型跨境电商企业的海外战略分析_孙智佳.docx", "dimension": "platform", "tags": []},
    {"id": "PLATFORM-商业生态系统视角下出口型跨境电商企业的海-061", "title": "Michael E. Porter, the father of competitive strategy, believes that enterprises", "content": "Michael E. Porter, the father of competitive strategy, believes that enterprises in different industries must choose one of concentration strategy, cost leadership strategy and differentiation strategy as  their corporate strategy. Moore  (1993)  was  the  first foreign researcher to propose the definition of business ecosystems, which breaks the limitations of the competitive strategy based on the division of industries in the past, that is to say, business ecosystems as a new business model no longer believes that \"the process of economic operation is to get rid of the weak\". That is to say,", "source": "platform/商业生态系统视角下出口型跨境电商企业的海外战略分析_孙智佳.docx", "dimension": "platform", "tags": []},
    {"id": "PLATFORM-商业生态系统视角下出口型跨境电商企业的海-062", "title": "4   Si Erxun Distributed Business Ecosystem Strategy: New Logic  of Digital Busi", "content": "4   Si Erxun Distributed Business Ecosystem Strategy: New Logic  of Digital Business and New Strategy for Enterprise Digital Transformation Tsinghua University Press 2023", "source": "platform/商业生态系统视角下出口型跨境电商企业的海外战略分析_孙智佳.docx", "dimension": "platform", "tags": []},
    {"id": "PLATFORM-商业生态系统视角下出口型跨境电商企业的海-063", "title": "and needed the assistance of others, and thus started the cooperation between Ap", "content": "and needed the assistance of others, and thus started the cooperation between Apple and  Microsoft.  That  is  to  say,  once  the  companies  in  the  ecosystem  destroy  the friendly and co-operative relationship, it will be unfavourable to anyone.MarcoIansiti et al. (2004) investigated the large enterprises such as Microsoft and Wal-Mart, and used the empirical method to prove once again that each company in the business ecosystem shares the fate of the whole system. And based on actual cases of business ecosystems of companies such as Intel, Microsoft, Apple, Google and Disney, they conclu", "source": "platform/商业生态系统视角下出口型跨境电商企业的海外战略分析_孙智佳.docx", "dimension": "platform", "tags": []},
    {"id": "PLATFORM-商业生态系统视角下出口型跨境电商企业的海-064", "title": "Foreign researchers generally agree that the collaboration of companies used in ", "content": "Foreign researchers generally agree that the collaboration of companies used in the  business  ecosystem  can  create   features   such  as  economies   of  scale   and complementary  mechanisms,  which  have  the  effect  of  significantly  reducing  the company\'s innovation and transaction costs. Generally speaking, many branch firms are self-centred and aim to adapt to the competitive market environment, forming a community of interest  which,  in  a  sense,  is  better  able  to  cater  to  the  needs  of customers.", "source": "platform/商业生态系统视角下出口型跨境电商企业的海外战略分析_孙智佳.docx", "dimension": "platform", "tags": []},
    {"id": "PLATFORM-商业生态系统视角下出口型跨境电商企业的海-065", "title": "Li  Dong  (2008)  classified  the   developing  business  ecosystem  into   thre", "content": "Li  Dong  (2008)  classified  the   developing  business  ecosystem  into   three dimensions: attraction, entry and growth, and conducted an empirical study on several major domestic and foreign enterprises as research objects.  By analysing the three dimensions, the business ecosystem was classified into vast grassland, cluster forest and  two  new  forest  types  of business  ecosystem.  Wu  Building  Materials  (2017) proposed that the evolution and development of business ecosystems is driven by the \"law of aggregation\", which is formed by the competition and collaboration between various ", "source": "platform/商业生态系统视角下出口型跨境电商企业的海外战略分析_孙智佳.docx", "dimension": "platform", "tags": []},
    {"id": "PLATFORM-商业生态系统视角下出口型跨境电商企业的海-066", "title": "rely.  Ning  Lianju  et  al.  (2020)  analysed  the  construction  of enterprise", "content": "rely.  Ning  Lianju  et  al.  (2020)  analysed  the  construction  of enterprise  business ecosystems  from  the  perspective  of transaction  costs,  thus  effectively  solving  the plague  of  information  asymmetry  between  enterprises.   He  pointed   out  that  the features  of  embedded  resources,  network  effects,  symbiosis,  and  co-evolution  in enterprise business ecosystems  are pivotal  in  solving  the  problems  of asymmetry, multi-level decision-making, and trust. Tao Rui and Zeng Ping (2021) put forward the business ecosystem model of Xiaomi\'s non-controlling investment pla", "source": "platform/商业生态系统视角下出口型跨境电商企业的海外战略分析_孙智佳.docx", "dimension": "platform", "tags": []},
    {"id": "PLATFORM-商业生态系统视角下出口型跨境电商企业的海-067", "title": "As successful leaders in the fierce competition of international cross-border e-", "content": "As successful leaders in the fierce competition of international cross-border e- commerce, the indicators of brand awareness, sales, and market share prove that the Temu and SHEIN platforms have achieved  great commercial success. However, as similar  competitors,  their  business  models  are   quite  different,   especially   in  the construction of business  ecosystems  such  as  supply  chain  strategies,  which  show different strategic directions. This paper will focus on comparing the same industry environment challenges, profitability risks and different strategies adopted for future s", "source": "platform/商业生态系统视角下出口型跨境电商企业的海外战略分析_孙智佳.docx", "dimension": "platform", "tags": []},
    {"id": "PLATFORM-商业生态系统视角下出口型跨境电商企业的海-068", "title": "Intrapopulation relationships refer to  the  interrelationships  that  exist  be", "content": "Intrapopulation relationships refer to  the  interrelationships  that  exist  between individuals within  a  population  of organisms.  These  individuals  compete  and  co - operate  with each other. Intra-population relationships  in cross-border e-commerce ecosystems refer to the relationships between individuals operating similar products or with the same  model.  They are  characterised  by intraspecific collaboration and intraspecific  struggle.\n\n2.2.1 Intraspecies collaboration", "source": "platform/商业生态系统视角下出口型跨境电商企业的海外战略分析_孙智佳.docx", "dimension": "platform", "tags": []},
    {"id": "PLATFORM-商业生态系统视角下出口型跨境电商企业的海-069", "title": "Intraspecific  collaboration  is  the  behaviour  of  organisms  that  divide   ", "content": "Intraspecific  collaboration  is  the  behaviour  of  organisms  that  divide   and collaborate with each other  in order to resist external aggression and thus maintain survival. For example, when geese migrate in autumn, in order to have enough energy to reach their destination, they collaborate with each other to form a formation and create  greater  momentum.  In  cross-border  e-commerce   ecosystems,  intraspecies collaboration  is  more  of an  internal  division  of  labour.   The  fundamental  reason affecting intraspecies collaboration is to share more resources of resources, thus bo", "source": "platform/商业生态系统视角下出口型跨境电商企业的海外战略分析_孙智佳.docx", "dimension": "platform", "tags": []},
    {"id": "PLATFORM-商业生态系统视角下出口型跨境电商企业的海-070", "title": "2.2.2 Intraspecific  competition", "content": "2.2.2 Intraspecific  competition\n\nThe behaviour of individuals of the same species who fight and kill each other over   resources   and   space    is   called   intraspecific   competition.    In   intraspecific competition,  the  weak  will  be  eliminated.  This  is  harmful  to  the  individuals  but beneficial to the population as a whole. The weaker individuals are eliminated and the stronger ones are maintained, which is beneficial for the evolution and prosperity of the  population.  Intraspecific  competition  in  cross-border  e-commerce  ecosystems refers to the behaviour of individu", "source": "platform/商业生态系统视角下出口型跨境电商企业的海外战略分析_孙智佳.docx", "dimension": "platform", "tags": []},
    {"id": "PLATFORM-商业生态系统视角下出口型跨境电商企业的海-071", "title": "example, in the cross-border e-commerce ecosystem, the number of cross-border e-", "content": "example, in the cross-border e-commerce ecosystem, the number of cross-border e- commerce  demanders  is  limited,  and  cross-border  e-commerce  providers  compete fiercely in terms of products and business models in order to compete for more cross- border e-commerce demanders and to take up more market share.\n\n2.2.3 Ecosystem boundary  analysis", "source": "platform/商业生态系统视角下出口型跨境电商企业的海外战略分析_孙智佳.docx", "dimension": "platform", "tags": []},
    {"id": "PLATFORM-商业生态系统视角下出口型跨境电商企业的海-072", "title": "Every  link   in  cross-border  e-commerce  transactions   has   the   existence", "content": "Every  link   in  cross-border  e-commerce  transactions   has   the   existence  of information flow, capital flow and logistics. They are closely linked, and these three are prerequisites and  interdependent.  The  logistics and capital of the enterprise  are one-way flows and are complementary. The flow of information is a two-way flow, which accompanies the logistics and capital flow and produce, in turn, they play a guiding role. And logistics and information flow to the flow of capital has the role of value contribution, reduce the cost of enterprises, speed up the flow of capital. Above", "source": "platform/商业生态系统视角下出口型跨境电商企业的海外战略分析_孙智佳.docx", "dimension": "platform", "tags": []},
    {"id": "PLATFORM-商业生态系统视角下出口型跨境电商企业的海-073", "title": "cross-border e-commerce provider\'s products or services. As  shown  in Figure 2.", "content": "cross-border e-commerce provider\'s products or services. As  shown  in Figure 2.1. Information asymmetry is the root cause of product, payment, and logistics problems in cross-border e-commerce. In the cross-border e-commerce ecosystem, the party that has  more  information  is  in an advantageous position in the  whole  transaction chain and obtains more profits, while the party with less access to information is in an unfavourable position. Information asymmetry leads to a variety of problems in the operation of cross-border  e-commerce,  so  in  order  to  reduce  the  problems  in  the tra", "source": "platform/商业生态系统视角下出口型跨境电商企业的海外战略分析_孙智佳.docx", "dimension": "platform", "tags": []},
    {"id": "PLATFORM-商业生态系统视角下出口型跨境电商企业的海-074", "title": "The concept of \"synergy\" was  first defined by the physicist  Hacken in  1977. S", "content": "The concept of \"synergy\" was  first defined by the physicist  Hacken in  1977. Synergism is the co-operation between the  components of a system that leads to a stable  state  of the  system.  Although  different  ecosystems  have  different   internal components and system structures,  from the perspective  of system equilibrium,  all systems are under the  internal and  external environments, the  internal elements of\n\n5   Global Cross-border E-commerce Brands Going Overseas Ecology Report", "source": "platform/商业生态系统视角下出口型跨境电商企业的海外战略分析_孙智佳.docx", "dimension": "platform", "tags": []},
    {"id": "PLATFORM-商业生态系统视角下出口型跨境电商企业的海-075", "title": "system co-operate and interact with each other, so as to make the system go from", "content": "system co-operate and interact with each other, so as to make the system go from a disordered state to an orderly and stable process. Within the system, if the elements can cooperate and  share  information  resources,  then  it  may  produce  the  effect  of \"1+1>2\", promoting the stable and healthy development of the system; if the elements of vicious competition, information sharing, although it seems that the short-term gain benefits for their own benefit, but in the long run, it will only exacerbate the speed of its  decline,  and   the  overall   impact  on  the   system\'s  stability.  T", "source": "platform/商业生态系统视角下出口型跨境电商企业的海外战略分析_孙智佳.docx", "dimension": "platform", "tags": []},
    {"id": "PLATFORM-商业生态系统视角下出口型跨境电商企业的海-076", "title": "(1) Development  of evolutionary  game  theory", "content": "(1) Development  of evolutionary  game  theory", "source": "platform/商业生态系统视角下出口型跨境电商企业的海外战略分析_孙智佳.docx", "dimension": "platform", "tags": []},
    {"id": "PLATFORM-商业生态系统视角下出口型跨境电商企业的海-077", "title": "Game theory first originated from the English \"GameTheory\", as early as more tha", "content": "Game theory first originated from the English \"GameTheory\", as early as more than 100 years ago, the game theory was initially applied in the chess game, in the 1960s the famous scientists Weng Ting will be applied in the ecological problems, and according  to  the  biological  evolution of the  law  of the  mutation  theory  and  the combination of the traditional game, and put forward the Reproduction of dynamic equations. Evolutionary game and Darwin\'s theory of evolution has a strong origin, in 1859, Darwin in the \"Origin of Species\" proposed that the biological individual by the influence", "source": "platform/商业生态系统视角下出口型跨境电商企业的海外战略分析_孙智佳.docx", "dimension": "platform", "tags": []},
    {"id": "PLATFORM-商业生态系统视角下出口型跨境电商企业的海-078", "title": "After sorting out the development process of evolutionary game, it can be seen t", "content": "After sorting out the development process of evolutionary game, it can be seen that: evolutionary game comes from traditional game but is different from traditional game. The similarity between evolutionary game and traditional game lies in that both", "source": "platform/商业生态系统视角下出口型跨境电商企业的海外战略分析_孙智佳.docx", "dimension": "platform", "tags": []},
    {"id": "PLATFORM-商业生态系统视角下出口型跨境电商企业的海-079", "title": "of them are strategy selection of game subjects to reach equilibrium state; diff", "content": "of them are strategy selection of game subjects to reach equilibrium state; difference lies in that: evolutionary game regards game subjects as \"limited rational man\", and both of game parties can adjust their own strategies at any time, so that the  game process  is  in dynamics;  while traditional game  evolution regards game subjects as \"completely  rational  man\",  and  the   game  process   is  static.  The  traditional  game evolution regards the  game  subject as  \"completely rational person\",  and  the  game process  is  static.  The   \"limited  rational  man\"  refers  to  the  fact  t", "source": "platform/商业生态系统视角下出口型跨境电商企业的海外战略分析_孙智佳.docx", "dimension": "platform", "tags": []},
    {"id": "PLATFORM-商业生态系统视角下出口型跨境电商企业的海-080", "title": "(2) The combination  of strategies  of the  subjects involved   in the game.", "content": "(2) The combination  of strategies  of the  subjects involved   in the game.\n\nFor the evolutionary game, the subjects involved in the game can be two or more. The subjects participating in the game have randomness in choosing corresponding strategies, so  when the strategy combination of the  game party changes,  the  game subject will have different gains or losses. And in the whole game process, the game party can change  its own strategy according to the strategy of other game subjects, which  can   increase  the  benefit  or  reduce   the   loss  accordingly.   Eventually,  the\n\nequilibriu", "source": "platform/商业生态系统视角下出口型跨境电商企业的海外战略分析_孙智佳.docx", "dimension": "platform", "tags": []},
    {"id": "PLATFORM-商业生态系统视角下出口型跨境电商企业的海-081", "title": "(3) The basic assumption of evolutionary game is that the subjects participating", "content": "(3) The basic assumption of evolutionary game is that the subjects participating in the game  are all  \"limited  rational man\".\n\nThat is: when the subject of the game began to play the game, due to their own reasons,  information  asymmetry  and  a  series  of  limitations,  to  choose  their  own beneficial strategy combinations. And with the further development of the evolution process, the evolution subject constantly adjusts  its own  strategy selection. At the same time, the probability of the evolution of the subject to choose each strategy is not the same, the gain or loss is not the sa", "source": "platform/商业生态系统视角下出口型跨境电商企业的海外战略分析_孙智佳.docx", "dimension": "platform", "tags": []},
    {"id": "PLATFORM-商业生态系统视角下出口型跨境电商企业的海-082", "title": "(4) Replication  of dynamic  equations.", "content": "(4) Replication  of dynamic  equations.\n\nAccording to  the  above  analysis,  it  can be  seen  that  when members of the system  are  playing  the  evolutionary  game,  they  can  adjust  their  own  strategies according to the strategy choices of other evolutionary subjects and then adjust their own strategies.  That  is,  the  strategy choice  in  the  evolutionary  game  is  always  in dynamic. Some scholars have found that the probability change of strategy selection of evolutionary subjects is regular and  can be quantified  uniformly by an equation, which  is the replication  dynamic  e", "source": "platform/商业生态系统视角下出口型跨境电商企业的海外战略分析_孙智佳.docx", "dimension": "platform", "tags": []},
    {"id": "PLATFORM-商业生态系统视角下出口型跨境电商企业的海-083", "title": "Because of the information, resources and other related  factors, make the subje", "content": "Because of the information, resources and other related  factors, make the subject of the game can not always be  in the dynamic change, but with the passage of time, will reach a kind of game subject are satisfied with the stable state. But this stable state is not static, with the change of strategy of the main body of the game and the influence of other factors, will make the system reach another stable state, this process is called  evolutionary  stable  equilibrium.\n\n2.5 Definition and development of cross-border e-commerce\n\n2.5.1 Definition of cross-border e-commerce", "source": "platform/商业生态系统视角下出口型跨境电商企业的海外战略分析_孙智佳.docx", "dimension": "platform", "tags": []},
    {"id": "PLATFORM-商业生态系统视角下出口型跨境电商企业的海-084", "title": "Cross-border   e-commerce   is    an   abbreviation   for   cross-border   elect", "content": "Cross-border   e-commerce   is    an   abbreviation   for   cross-border   electronic commerce, with a distinction between a broad and a narrow sense. Broad cross-border e-commerce  refers  to  the   commercial  activities   of different  transaction  subjects engaged in cross-border trade through modern electronic information technology and means of communication. Cross-border e-commerce in the narrow sense refers to a new type of commodity trading activities in which different trading subjects, through electronic  modern  electronic   information  technology  and  communication  means, reach", "source": "platform/商业生态系统视角下出口型跨境电商企业的海外战略分析_孙智佳.docx", "dimension": "platform", "tags": []},
    {"id": "PLATFORM-商业生态系统视角下出口型跨境电商企业的海-085", "title": "Upstream production suppliers,  midstream cross-border e-commerce platforms and ", "content": "Upstream production suppliers,  midstream cross-border e-commerce platforms and  downstream  support  service  providers  and  sellers,  covering  a  wide  range  of aspects such as products, technology, transactions, payment, logistics, warehousing, etc.,    gradually    forming    a    three-dimensional    ecosystem.     Suppliers    include: manufacturers, foreign trade enterprises, e-commerce sellers. Buyers include: traders,", "source": "platform/商业生态系统视角下出口型跨境电商企业的海外战略分析_孙智佳.docx", "dimension": "platform", "tags": []},
    {"id": "PLATFORM-商业生态系统视角下出口型跨境电商企业的海-086", "title": "purchasers and individual consumers. Cross-border e-commerce platforms and servi", "content": "purchasers and individual consumers. Cross-border e-commerce platforms and service providers include: multinational third-party platforms, customs clearance, tax rebates, foreign exchange clearance, freight forwarders, shipping, cross-border courier, parcels, credit cards, information technology, human resources, translators and other service providers,  payment  platforms,   financial  institutions,  and   insurance  companies.  In addition,  customs,  commerce,  taxation  and  foreign  exchange  departments  are  also important  parts of the cross-border e-commerce  ecosystem.\n\n2.5.2 Classif", "source": "platform/商业生态系统视角下出口型跨境电商企业的海外战略分析_孙智佳.docx", "dimension": "platform", "tags": []},
    {"id": "PLATFORM-商业生态系统视角下出口型跨境电商企业的海-087", "title": "According  to  the  type  of transaction,  cross-border  e-commerce  mode  can  ", "content": "According  to  the  type  of transaction,  cross-border  e-commerce  mode  can  be divided into: B2B, B2C, C2C and other basic modes. B2B (Business-to-Business) is a business model of exchanging and transmitting data and information and carrying out trading activities between enterprises and enterprises through a dedicated network or the Internet. Representative enterprises include: Alibaba International, Made-in-China, Global Sources, Dunhuang.com, DaLong.com, etc. B2C (Business-to-Customer) is a business  activity  mode  in  which  enterprises  in  different borders  sell products  and servi", "source": "platform/商业生态系统视角下出口型跨境电商企业的海外战略分析_孙智佳.docx", "dimension": "platform", "tags": []},
    {"id": "PLATFORM-商业生态系统视角下出口型跨境电商企业的海-088", "title": "According to the division of the  operating body,  the cross-border e-commerce m", "content": "According to the division of the  operating body,  the cross-border e-commerce model can be divided  into: platform-type,  self-supporting,  hybrid  (platform +  self- supporting). Platform-type mode, that is, by the third-party open platform through the online mall, integration of logistics, payment, operation and other service resources to attract   domestic   and   foreign   merchants   stationed    in   the   mode   of  operation. Representative enterprises  are: Amazon, Dunhuang,  Sell-through,  eBay and  so on.", "source": "platform/商业生态系统视角下出口型跨境电商企业的海外战略分析_孙智佳.docx", "dimension": "platform", "tags": []},
    {"id": "PLATFORM-商业生态系统视角下出口型跨境电商企业的海-089", "title": "Self-operated  cross-border  e-commerce  platform  refers  to  the   mode   in  ", "content": "Self-operated  cross-border  e-commerce  platform  refers  to  the   mode   in  which  e- commerce enterprises earn profits by building platforms and integrating supply chain resources  to  sell  products  and  services  directly  through  online  channels.  Mainly include:  Lanting,  Koala,  Globalbuy,   Little  Red Book and so on.", "source": "platform/商业生态系统视角下出口型跨境电商企业的海外战略分析_孙智佳.docx", "dimension": "platform", "tags": []},
    {"id": "PLATFORM-商业生态系统视角下出口型跨境电商企业的海-090", "title": "According to the  flow of goods,  it  can be  divided  into  export  cross-borde", "content": "According to the  flow of goods,  it  can be  divided  into  export  cross-border e- commerce  and  import  cross-border  e-commerce.  Export  cross-border  e-commerce refers to the enterprises through e-commerce to display goods, enter into transactions and complete the goods or services delivered to overseas importers of trade activities, is  the  mainstream  of cross-border  e-commerce   in  China.  Import  cross-border  e- commerce mainly refers to the overseas goods through e-commerce sales to China\'s importing body of the activities, at present, mainly for the import platform before the ", "source": "platform/商业生态系统视角下出口型跨境电商企业的海外战略分析_孙智佳.docx", "dimension": "platform", "tags": []},
    {"id": "PLATFORM-商业生态系统视角下出口型跨境电商企业的海-091", "title": "2.5.3 Overview of cross-border e-commerce development in China", "content": "2.5.3 Overview of cross-border e-commerce development in China\n\n(1) Characteristics  of cross-border e-commerce  development  in  China", "source": "platform/商业生态系统视角下出口型跨境电商企业的海外战略分析_孙智佳.docx", "dimension": "platform", "tags": []},
    {"id": "PLATFORM-商业生态系统视角下出口型跨境电商企业的海-092", "title": "Firstly, relative to developed countries, China started late. Accompanied by the", "content": "Firstly, relative to developed countries, China started late. Accompanied by the development of Internet technology and the continuous advancement of the globalised economy, e-commerce has gained significant development in many countries around the world, and at the same time effectively driven the development of cross-border e- commerce, which at the present stage has gradually become an important part of the development of China\'s foreign trade. The development of cross-border e-commerce in China relative to other developed countries, although it has the characteristics ofa late start, but t", "source": "platform/商业生态系统视角下出口型跨境电商企业的海外战略分析_孙智佳.docx", "dimension": "platform", "tags": []},
    {"id": "PLATFORM-商业生态系统视角下出口型跨境电商企业的海-093", "title": "Second,  the  global  complexity  of the  supply  chain.   Due  to  the  continu", "content": "Second,  the  global  complexity  of the  supply  chain.   Due  to  the  continuous development of Internet information technology, domestic enterprises are no  longer affected by regional spatial restrictions, and their industrial products and services have been  gradually  moving  towards  the  world  to  carry  out  multi-field,  multi-faceted, multi-level  and  omni-directional  trade  activities  on  a   global  scale.  The  Internet enables foreign consumers to buy and sell overseas commodities with the help of the Internet, and  consumers  hope  that  they can  meet  their  own  shoppin", "source": "platform/商业生态系统视角下出口型跨境电商企业的海外战略分析_孙智佳.docx", "dimension": "platform", "tags": []},
    {"id": "PLATFORM-商业生态系统视角下出口型跨境电商企业的海-094", "title": "(2) Impact of the development  of cross-border e-commerce  in China", "content": "(2) Impact of the development  of cross-border e-commerce  in China", "source": "platform/商业生态系统视角下出口型跨境电商企业的海外战略分析_孙智佳.docx", "dimension": "platform", "tags": []},
    {"id": "PLATFORM-商业生态系统视角下出口型跨境电商企业的海-095", "title": "Cross-border e-commerce  includes both cross-border  imports  and cross-border e", "content": "Cross-border e-commerce  includes both cross-border  imports  and cross-border exports;  the   impact  of  cross-border   e-commerce  has   import  and   export  trade differentials. Cross-border  imports can  increase  the  domestic commodity category, and cross-border exports can make Chinese manufacturing out of the country. Cross- border exports are relatively helpful to China\'s economic development, the country is now also more supportive of this piece, the emergence of cross-border e-commerce platforms will be trading offline to online,  more convenient and  more visual. 2013 August the ", "source": "platform/商业生态系统视角下出口型跨境电商企业的海外战略分析_孙智佳.docx", "dimension": "platform", "tags": []},
