    {"id": "PLATFORM-商业生态系统视角下出口型跨境电商企业的海-195", "title": "The  strategic   choices  made  by  enterprises   in  the  cross-border  e-comme", "content": "The  strategic   choices  made  by  enterprises   in  the  cross-border  e-commerce ecosystem are affected by information resources, and when the information between enterprises  is  not  smooth  or  unequal,  enterprises  tend  to  adopt  unilateral  egoistic behaviours, thus affecting the stability of the cross-border e-commerce ecosystem as a whole.The policy and legal risks encountered by Temu and SHEIN in the competition for  the   U.S.   market  are  an  important  revelation.   As  cross-border  e-commerce platforms   with  similar   ecological  niches,   more   and   more   intense   i", "source": "platform/商业生态系统视角下出口型跨境电商企业的海外战略分析_孙智佳.docx", "dimension": "platform", "tags": []},
    {"id": "PLATFORM-商业生态系统视角下出口型跨境电商企业的海-196", "title": "benefits   of  enterprises,   which   in   turn   promotes   the   sustainable  ", "content": "benefits   of  enterprises,   which   in   turn   promotes   the   sustainable   and   healthy development  of the  cross-border  e-commerce  ecosystem.  For  core  and  supporting enterprises, promoting the sharing of information resources between enterprises and removing information barriers between enterprises can reduce  their operating costs. For   example:   information   resource   sharing   between   cross-border   e-commerce platforms and cross-border logistics enterprises, cross-border e-commerce platforms will dynamically update the commodity logistics information through the platfo", "source": "platform/商业生态系统视角下出口型跨境电商企业的海外战略分析_孙智佳.docx", "dimension": "platform", "tags": []},
    {"id": "PLATFORM-商业生态系统视角下出口型跨境电商企业的海-197", "title": "Because SHEIN once occupied as much as 75 per cent of the US market share, it ha", "content": "Because SHEIN once occupied as much as 75 per cent of the US market share, it has encountered very serious targeting from the US government and enterprises in the US, such as SHEIN\'s efforts to go public in the US, the IPO plan has been repeatedly blocked by the US government and capital. SHEIN\'s response strategy is to acquire shares of international apparel brand giants, move its headquarters to Singapore, and strive to build  its  image  to  a  more  internationalised  one,  downplaying the original Chinese  corporate elements  to cater to the preferences  of overseas capital.\n\n5.2 Optimisa", "source": "platform/商业生态系统视角下出口型跨境电商企业的海外战略分析_孙智佳.docx", "dimension": "platform", "tags": []},
    {"id": "PLATFORM-商业生态系统视角下出口型跨境电商企业的海-198", "title": "As mentioned earlier, the largest number of complaints from consumers in the Eur", "content": "As mentioned earlier, the largest number of complaints from consumers in the European and  American markets about  Temu  and  SHEIN  is  the  low  efficiency of logistics and the long waiting time to receive goods. In for the cross-border logistics link encountered many problems, can be solved through the overseas warehouse. The emergence  of overseas  warehouses  has  greatly  facilitated  the  development  of the cross-border e-commerce industry. Overseas warehouse refers to the cross-border e- commerce platform to build warehouses  in overseas countries or regions,  so as to store a certain", "source": "platform/商业生态系统视角下出口型跨境电商企业的海外战略分析_孙智佳.docx", "dimension": "platform", "tags": []},
    {"id": "PLATFORM-商业生态系统视角下出口型跨境电商企业的海-199", "title": "returned directly to the local overseas warehouse, reducing the link of cross-bo", "content": "returned directly to the local overseas warehouse, reducing the link of cross-border customs clearance  and commodity  inspection  when the  goods are returned  to China.", "source": "platform/商业生态系统视角下出口型跨境电商企业的海外战略分析_孙智佳.docx", "dimension": "platform", "tags": []},
    {"id": "PLATFORM-商业生态系统视角下出口型跨境电商企业的海-200", "title": "Improving the establishment and management of overseas warehouses can go a long ", "content": "Improving the establishment and management of overseas warehouses can go a long  way  in   improving  consumer   satisfaction  and  thus   cross-border  transaction volumes. SHEIN has several overseas transit warehouses around the world, but only receives  consumer  returns and  does  not  ship  them.  Therefore,  SHEIN  is  building several  overseas  warehouses   in  the   U.S.   In  2023,   the   distribution   centre   in Whitestown, Indiana, which occupies more than 1 million sq. ft. of space, will be in operation,   shortening   shipping  time  by  four  days.   Temu   has  also   starte", "source": "platform/商业生态系统视角下出口型跨境电商企业的海外战略分析_孙智佳.docx", "dimension": "platform", "tags": []},
    {"id": "PLATFORM-商业生态系统视角下出口型跨境电商企业的海-201", "title": "5.2.2 Establishment  of strategic logistics alliances", "content": "5.2.2 Establishment  of strategic logistics alliances\n\nIn  cross-border  logistics,  if cross-border  e-commerce  or  logistics  companies build logistics infrastructure alone, they will face a huge cost problem. SHEIN\'s goods transport  is  jointly  completed  by  several  logistics  companies.   According  to   the research conducted by  Transport  Link Intelligence,  in  terms of domestic  logistics, SHEIN will contract  logistics to  SF  and Cross  in  addition to  its  own logistics. In addition to its own logistics, SHEIN has contracted out its domestic logistics to SF and  Crossing,  wi", "source": "platform/商业生态系统视角下出口型跨境电商企业的海外战略分析_孙智佳.docx", "dimension": "platform", "tags": []},
    {"id": "PLATFORM-商业生态系统视角下出口型跨境电商企业的海-202", "title": "1/3 of the total business within Guangdong province.202  In July 2012,  SHEIN  a", "content": "1/3 of the total business within Guangdong province.202  In July 2012,  SHEIN  also signed a  strategic  co-operation agreement with China  Southern Airlines  Logistics, which  is  responsible   for  the   domestic  direct  mail  business.   95%  of  SHEIN\'s merchandise worldwide  is  sent  from its central warehouse  in  Foshan.  There  are  9 distribution warehouses  in Foshan, with a warehouse storage capacity of about  30 million pieces  and  about  400,000-500,000  SKUs;  overseas  transit  warehouses  are located in many countries such as Saudi Arabia, Dubai, Italy, Australia, Vietnam, e", "source": "platform/商业生态系统视角下出口型跨境电商企业的海外战略分析_孙智佳.docx", "dimension": "platform", "tags": []},
    {"id": "PLATFORM-商业生态系统视角下出口型跨境电商企业的海-203", "title": "Temu\'s strategy is relatively different, only domestic shipping costs are shared", "content": "Temu\'s strategy is relatively different, only domestic shipping costs are shared by the  merchant  and   Temu,  while  other  logistics  costs  are  borne  by  Temu.Temu merchants on the platform mainly have two models: VMI model (Vendor Managed Inventory) and JIT model (Just In Time). VMI mode, which stands for \"stock first, then sell on the shelves\" mode of stock preparation. Sellers need to apply to Temu for stocking first, after getting the warehouse space, sellers will send the goods to Temu\'s warehouse, Temu is responsible for warehousing; then Temu will handle the shipment according to ", "source": "platform/商业生态系统视角下出口型跨境电商企业的海外战略分析_孙智佳.docx", "dimension": "platform", "tags": []},
    {"id": "PLATFORM-商业生态系统视角下出口型跨境电商企业的海-204", "title": "SHEIN and Temu attach great importance to the service quality and efficiency of ", "content": "SHEIN and Temu attach great importance to the service quality and efficiency of logistics, and the huge logistics costs also limit profitability. Therefore, logistics co - operation  between  cross-border   e-commerce   or   logistics   enterprises   based   on", "source": "platform/商业生态系统视角下出口型跨境电商企业的海外战略分析_孙智佳.docx", "dimension": "platform", "tags": []},
    {"id": "PLATFORM-商业生态系统视角下出口型跨境电商企业的海-205", "title": "economies  of scale, joint  construction of logistics  facilities  and  the  for", "content": "economies  of scale, joint  construction of logistics  facilities  and  the  formation  of logistics strategic alliances can largely reduce the cost of cross-border logistics. For example, multiple cross-border e-commerce or logistics enterprises form an alliance and  together  invest  in building or renting logistics  infrastructure  such as  overseas warehouses and border warehouses, and jointly set up a logistics and warehousing centre  at  home  and  abroad.  Member  enterprises  in  the  alliance  can  transport commodities  to  foreign  logistics  and  distribution  centres   for  storag", "source": "platform/商业生态系统视角下出口型跨境电商企业的海外战略分析_孙智佳.docx", "dimension": "platform", "tags": []},
    {"id": "PLATFORM-商业生态系统视角下出口型跨境电商企业的海-206", "title": "5.3 Corporate  value proposition  and ecosystem optimisation", "content": "5.3 Corporate  value proposition  and ecosystem optimisation\n\n5.3.1 corporate  value proposition", "source": "platform/商业生态系统视角下出口型跨境电商企业的海外战略分析_孙智佳.docx", "dimension": "platform", "tags": []},
    {"id": "PLATFORM-商业生态系统视角下出口型跨境电商企业的海-207", "title": "In the past,  many  cross-border  e-commerce  enterprises  in  China  did  not p", "content": "In the past,  many  cross-border  e-commerce  enterprises  in  China  did  not pay attention to the construction of corporate  values. On the one hand, some of them believe that the promotion of brand overseas is limited to the development strategy of large enterprises, and their own development of brand overseas is still very long-term. From that perspective, many cross-border e-commerce enterprises have little interest in brand building, thus affecting their development speed. On the other hand, many domestic  cross-border  e-commerce  enterprises  choose   to  go  overseas  only  after enco", "source": "platform/商业生态系统视角下出口型跨境电商企业的海外战略分析_孙智佳.docx", "dimension": "platform", "tags": []},
    {"id": "PLATFORM-商业生态系统视角下出口型跨境电商企业的海-208", "title": "completes its internal strategic deployment before launching its products in the", "content": "completes its internal strategic deployment before launching its products in the market. Firstly,  SHEIN  clearly understands that the  future  market  competition  is  inevitably brand competition; secondly, SHEIN chooses the target market and target group, and clearly  defines  the  path  for  the  brand   to  go   to  sea;  thirdly,   it  builds  a  perfect organisational  structure;  and  fourthly,  it  establishes  the  operation  mode  of the independent station, which is in direct contact with the consumers. These measures have enabled  SHEIN to successfully  lay an advantage  in the in", "source": "platform/商业生态系统视角下出口型跨境电商企业的海外战略分析_孙智佳.docx", "dimension": "platform", "tags": []},
    {"id": "PLATFORM-商业生态系统视角下出口型跨境电商企业的海-209", "title": "Temu\'s  corporate  values  are  the result of exploring  cross-border e-commerce", "content": "Temu\'s  corporate  values  are  the result of exploring  cross-border e-commerce technology and  model innovation, empowering Chinese  factories,  and  Poundland\'s desire to create more value for consumers and merchants. And the extension of Temu is to extend this value creation to enterprises going overseas. Taking manufacturing SMEs  as  an  example,  Temu  opens  a   new  door  for  the  globalisation  of Chinese manufacturing. Temu  is  based  on  helping  Chinese  enterprises  to  achieve  revenue growth and create a second growth pole for going overseas, the key lies in the fact that Pin", "source": "platform/商业生态系统视角下出口型跨境电商企业的海外战略分析_孙智佳.docx", "dimension": "platform", "tags": []},
    {"id": "PLATFORM-商业生态系统视角下出口型跨境电商企业的海-210", "title": "also another major advantage of Temu: with Jinduoduo\'s experience in e-commerce ", "content": "also another major advantage of Temu: with Jinduoduo\'s experience in e-commerce business, Temu has a strong ability to find people  for goods, and Temu believes that the essence of the platform business is to benefit others as well as oneself, and Temu\'s team is using the evolution of cross-border e-commerce methodology to help Chinese manufacturing to reap multiple dividends. Lowering the threshold of entry for cross - border business is conducive for SMEs to carry forward their supply chain capabilities and overcome the sales difficulties of going overseas.Under  Temu\'s  fully  managed model", "source": "platform/商业生态系统视角下出口型跨境电商企业的海外战略分析_孙智佳.docx", "dimension": "platform", "tags": []},
    {"id": "PLATFORM-商业生态系统视角下出口型跨境电商企业的海-211", "title": "5.3.2 Improvement  of regulatory  mechanisms", "content": "5.3.2 Improvement  of regulatory  mechanisms", "source": "platform/商业生态系统视角下出口型跨境电商企业的海外战略分析_孙智佳.docx", "dimension": "platform", "tags": []},
    {"id": "PLATFORM-商业生态系统视角下出口型跨境电商企业的海-212", "title": "Cross-border  e-commerce  platforms   need  to   build  an  honest  environmenta", "content": "Cross-border  e-commerce  platforms   need  to   build  an  honest  environmental regulation mechanism to reward and punish relevant enterprises, and then regulate the behavioural activities of all subjects in the system. Research shows that cross-border e-commerce platforms improve the punishment of bad suppliers, which is not only conducive to protecting the rights and  interests of consumer populations, but also enhances the enthusiasm of consumer participation, and thus creates a good business environment. Cross-border e-commerce platforms can start from the following points, first,   cros", "source": "platform/商业生态系统视角下出口型跨境电商企业的海外战略分析_孙智佳.docx", "dimension": "platform", "tags": []},
    {"id": "PLATFORM-商业生态系统视角下出口型跨境电商企业的海-213", "title": "deposit to  restrain  the  suppliers, but  also  once  the  suppliers  choose  t", "content": "deposit to  restrain  the  suppliers, but  also  once  the  suppliers  choose  to  fraudulent behaviour, the cross-border e-commerce platform can charge a certain percentage of additional  costs,  and  require  the  suppliers  to   make  certain  compensation  to  the consumers.  Thirdly,  the  cross-border  e-commerce  platform  can  set  up  consumer complaint  channels  and  rewards  for  consumers  who   actively  participate   in  the complaints, so as to make the consumer complaints more convenient and quick and higher participation, and to realise the double supervision of consumers  an", "source": "platform/商业生态系统视角下出口型跨境电商企业的海外战略分析_孙智佳.docx", "dimension": "platform", "tags": []},
    {"id": "PLATFORM-商业生态系统视角下出口型跨境电商企业的海-214", "title": "In the face of numerous quality complaints from U.S. consumers, Temu\'s quality c", "content": "In the face of numerous quality complaints from U.S. consumers, Temu\'s quality control  of suppliers  is  based  on  encouragement  and  guidance,  supplemented  by penalties. Temu insists on giving  merchants partial quality after-sales  responsibility relief on the basis of the original after-sales service rules. Temu has the right to deal with after-sales quality orders belonging to  merchants\' responsibility  in  accordance with different grades based on the quality of the goods scores. Specific judging rules are as follows: firstly, products with quality scores of 90 to  100 are defined a", "source": "platform/商业生态系统视角下出口型跨境电商企业的海外战略分析_孙智佳.docx", "dimension": "platform", "tags": []},
    {"id": "PLATFORM-商业生态系统视角下出口型跨境电商企业的海-215", "title": "payment for the order, and the seller will pay 1.5 per cent of the declared pric", "content": "payment for the order, and the seller will pay 1.5 per cent of the declared price to the merchant for the after-sale quality problems. Sellers in accordance with the declared price of 1.5 times to bear the compensation;  Third,  the  quality  of 60  points  to 70 points  of  the  product   is  defined  as  substandard  paragraph,   if  the   substandard paragraph after-sales quality problems, the penalty is: not settled the order payment, the seller in accordance with the declared price of 2.5 times to bear the compensation; Fourth, the quality of 0 points to 60 points of the product is define", "source": "platform/商业生态系统视角下出口型跨境电商企业的海外战略分析_孙智佳.docx", "dimension": "platform", "tags": []},
    {"id": "PLATFORM-商业生态系统视角下出口型跨境电商企业的海-216", "title": "5.3.3 Widening the ecosystem of marketing  channels", "content": "5.3.3 Widening the ecosystem of marketing  channels\n\nSearch engine promotion is the most direct and effective mainstream promotion mode of online marketing. As overseas consumers are used to shopping through PC and search engines, Temu has placed a large number of paid search, display ads and", "source": "platform/商业生态系统视角下出口型跨境电商企业的海外战略分析_孙智佳.docx", "dimension": "platform", "tags": []},
    {"id": "PLATFORM-商业生态系统视角下出口型跨境电商企业的海-217", "title": "video ads on Google, thus optimising the search engine marketing strategy to inc", "content": "video ads on Google, thus optimising the search engine marketing strategy to increase brand  exposure  and  promote  conversion.  Therefore,  to  optimise  search  engine marketing  strategies  to  increase  brand   exposure  and  drive  conversions,   TEMU provides overseas consumers with the fastest way to a brand, i.e. creating a standalone website. The operation of a stand-alone website helps branding and unification, and reduces the cost  of product testing.  TEMU  not only  collects personal  information from the website, such as consumption history, favourite records, time spent on the ", "source": "platform/商业生态系统视角下出口型跨境电商企业的海外战略分析_孙智佳.docx", "dimension": "platform", "tags": []},
    {"id": "PLATFORM-商业生态系统视角下出口型跨境电商企业的海-218", "title": "Social media is another way for TEMU to promote its brand. Currently, TEMU is wi", "content": "Social media is another way for TEMU to promote its brand. Currently, TEMU is widely promoted through the following four aspects. Firstly, TEMU uses a matrixed approach to build up its accounts, whereby large and small accounts drive traffic to each other. In addition,  TEMU  has  more  than 20  sub-accounts,  each of which  is divided into different sections, and draws traffic through the homepage of the main account. Secondly, TEMU has opened \"localised\" accounts in different countries and regions, and the clothing styles and model poses of TEMU\'s sub-accounts have been adjusted  according  ", "source": "platform/商业生态系统视角下出口型跨境电商企业的海外战略分析_孙智佳.docx", "dimension": "platform", "tags": []},
    {"id": "PLATFORM-商业生态系统视角下出口型跨境电商企业的海-219", "title": "With the rapid development of network economy, online channels can provide more ", "content": "With the rapid development of network economy, online channels can provide more  dividends  for  the  development  of enterprises,  but  the  promotion  of offline marketing  should   not  be   ignored.   Therefore,   China\'s   cross-border   e-commerce enterprises  take  the  integration of \"online  +  offline\" omni-channel  marketing as a strategic  focus  to   promote  the  brand   development  of  cross-border  e-commerce", "source": "platform/商业生态系统视角下出口型跨境电商企业的海外战略分析_孙智佳.docx", "dimension": "platform", "tags": []},
    {"id": "PLATFORM-商业生态系统视角下出口型跨境电商企业的海-220", "title": "enterprises and expand the influence of the brand in the overseas market. In ter", "content": "enterprises and expand the influence of the brand in the overseas market. In terms of online  marketing,  with  the  development  of  mobile  Internet  technology,  people\'s demand  for  social  networks   is  also   growing.   Social  media   as  a  new  type   of communication is widely used in various industries and has become a necessary way and  development  trend   of  online  marketing  promotion.   Firstly,  cross-border  e- commerce enterprises can strengthen interaction with fans through official platforms of social media operation such as Facebook, Instagram, etc.,  such as introduc", "source": "platform/商业生态系统视角下出口型跨境电商企业的海外战略分析_孙智佳.docx", "dimension": "platform", "tags": []},
    {"id": "PLATFORM-商业生态系统视角下出口型跨境电商企业的海-221", "title": "(3) Affiliate  marketing promotion", "content": "(3) Affiliate  marketing promotion", "source": "platform/商业生态系统视角下出口型跨境电商企业的海外战略分析_孙智佳.docx", "dimension": "platform", "tags": []},
    {"id": "PLATFORM-商业生态系统视角下出口型跨境电商企业的海-222", "title": "TEMU\'s \"Affiliate Marketing Programme\" encourages more and more users to volunta", "content": "TEMU\'s \"Affiliate Marketing Programme\" encourages more and more users to voluntarily participate  in brand promotion in the  form of rebates,  thus achieving a win-win situation. In terms of offline marketing, cross-border e-commerce companies need  to  create  multi-scene  interactive  experience  shops  that  focus  on  consumers\' senses. Although Internet technology has broken the boundaries of time and space, mobile devices enable consumers to  more conveniently and quickly access product brand  information directly.  However,  for  consumers,  offline  shops  are  always  the most  impres", "source": "platform/商业生态系统视角下出口型跨境电商企业的海外战略分析_孙智佳.docx", "dimension": "platform", "tags": []},
    {"id": "PLATFORM-商业生态系统视角下出口型跨境电商企业的海-223", "title": "services,  and  enhance  the  interaction  between  the  experience  and  the  b", "content": "services,  and  enhance  the  interaction  between  the  experience  and  the  brand.  For example, sponsoring student clubs to enter the campus to bring the brand closer to consumers, win their trust, and allow them to enjoy a higher-quality and more refined service  experience.  Whether  it  is  online  or  offline  marketing,  cross-border  e- commerce companies need to start from the customer\'s point of view in order to  get the best marketing and brand image. In the current situation, the epidemic has led to challenges for brick-and-mortar shops, and cross-border e-commerce enterprises ca", "source": "platform/商业生态系统视角下出口型跨境电商企业的海外战略分析_孙智佳.docx", "dimension": "platform", "tags": []},
    {"id": "PLATFORM-商业生态系统视角下出口型跨境电商企业的海-224", "title": "The   rapid   development   of  cross-border   e-commerce   in   China   has   b", "content": "The   rapid   development   of  cross-border   e-commerce   in   China   has   been accompanied by numerous challenges. This paper seeks to elucidate the composition and operational dynamics of cross-border e-commerce platform ecosystems through the  lens of business ecosystem theory and relevant  frameworks.  By examining the prevailing state of China\'s cross-border e-commerce platform ecosystem, this paper endeavors to identify  extant  issues  and underlying  causes therein.", "source": "platform/商业生态系统视角下出口型跨境电商企业的海外战略分析_孙智佳.docx", "dimension": "platform", "tags": []},
    {"id": "PLATFORM-商业生态系统视角下出口型跨境电商企业的海-225", "title": "Drawing upon insights from domestic and international cross-border e-commerce re", "content": "Drawing upon insights from domestic and international cross-border e-commerce research, this paper scrutinizes the strategic responses of key industry players, namely Temu,  within  the  shared  ecosystem  of the  cross-border  e-commerce  marketplace. Despite operating within the same competitive landscape, Temu has adopted divergent strategic  trajectories,  reflecting  variances  in their  foundational  value  propositions.\n\nTemu\'s platform business model is characterized by a pronounced emphasis on nurturing the domestic supply chain ecosystem. This strategic orientation aligns with the co", "source": "platform/商业生态系统视角下出口型跨境电商企业的海外战略分析_孙智佳.docx", "dimension": "platform", "tags": []},
    {"id": "PLATFORM-商业生态系统视角下出口型跨境电商企业的海-226", "title": "Owing to the author\'s research level and time constraints, this paper exhibits t", "content": "Owing to the author\'s research level and time constraints, this paper exhibits the following  deficiencies.\n\nFirstly, given the limited space in the article, incomplete data collection, and the author\'s own deficiencies  in  interdisciplinary  expertise,  this  paper only presents a relatively simplistic analysis  framework  rooted  in ecological  theory,  which  cannot provide a comprehensive analysis of the overseas strategies of export-oriented cross- border e-commerce enterprises.\n\nSecondly, the article focuses solely on Temu as a case studies, which may lack representativeness in its anal", "source": "platform/商业生态系统视角下出口型跨境电商企业的海外战略分析_孙智佳.docx", "dimension": "platform", "tags": []},
    {"id": "PLATFORM-商业生态系统视角下出口型跨境电商企业的海-227", "title": "Lastly, due to access limitations, the article includes fewer citations of relev", "content": "Lastly, due to access limitations, the article includes fewer citations of relevant data,  predominantly   focusing   on  theoretical  analysis.  Additional  supplementary research is needed for empirical  testing  data.\n\nTherefore,    more   representative    export-oriented   cross-border   e-commerce enterprises using the existing analytical framework can be added into future research, which  may  offer  more  precise  and  detailed  actionable  recommendations  for  their development.\n\nAsosheh, A. ,    Shahidi-Nejad, H. , &    Khodkari, H. . (2012). A model ofa localized cross-border e-com", "source": "platform/商业生态系统视角下出口型跨境电商企业的海外战略分析_孙智佳.docx", "dimension": "platform", "tags": []},
